# ── Compass Forge / local state ────────────────────────────────────────────
.compass-forge/
*.swp
.DS_Store
._*

# ── NEVER COMMIT: model weights ────────────────────────────────────────────
# GGUFs live on multivac at /srv/models and /srv/bench/models. They are pinned
# by sha256 + bytes in data/raw/e12/env-manifest.json, which is what belongs in
# git. A single one of these is 17-25 GB.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

# ── NEVER COMMIT: logits / KV dumps ────────────────────────────────────────
# SSA KL-divergence base files are ~11 GB each.
*.kld
*.logits

# ── NEVER COMMIT: container / image material ───────────────────────────────
# Images are pinned by RepoDigest in env-manifest.json — that is the provenance
# record; the layers themselves are re-pullable and must not enter git.
*.tar
*.oci
*.squashfs
Dockerfile.lock
images/
containers/

# ── NEVER COMMIT: bulk corpora and generated pads ──────────────────────────
# Regenerate with experiments/prebuild_pads.py; manifests ARE tracked.
corpus.txt
pads/
*.pad
wikitext2-*.txt

# ── Large / regenerable run output ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Server logs can reach hundreds of MB. The per-cell metadata in the tsweep and
# ssa JSONs records each log's path and byte count, which is the durable record.
*.serverlog
server-timings/
power-log.csv
*.log.gz
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv*/

# Anything above 5 MB should be justified in a commit message before being
# force-added. Check with:  git ls-files | xargs du -k | sort -rn | head

# ── Agent operating instructions ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Held back from the public repository for now (owner decision, 2026-09-09).
# These describe how the campaign was driven, not what it measured. They are
# intended for a later release once reviewed; nothing in them is a credential.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
